			<div class="content" id="post-content-3813367">
									

<p>I'm afraid this is gonna have to be a -1 from me.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>There are quite a few grammar and clinical tone errors scattered throughout the article:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>instances do not have to materialize at every single time marker;</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>After approximately thirty-two minutes and twenty-four seconds</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Attempts to translate the binary into anything meaningful always results in gibberish; this hints that the code is, indeed, meaningless. Testing is still ongoing, but is considered low-priority.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Are a few examples. For reference, I would replace each one respectively with:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>instances do not necessarily materialize each day;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sounds a bit better in my opinion, as 'do not have to' makes it seem like some sort of rule, and 'time markers' is an odd way to phrase it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After approximately thirty minutes</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The original sounded off to me because of how specific it was - despite you saying 'approximately'. This works better, or you could just get rid of the approximately.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Binary translates into seemingly random strings of numbers and letters.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Don't use 'gibberish' in a clinical document, and the hinting at meaningless binary bit is pointless. Its very obviously meaningless from the start.</p>
<p>Like I said, these are just a few examples - there are certainly more bits needing improvement. But another issue is that it's simply too long.</p>
<p>More text doesn't necessarily make a better article. As is, its quite difficult to get through, and would be vastly improved by cutting out some of the filler, particularly in the test logs. There are also some conceptual issues, but to be honest I've never been great at concepts in general.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I would recommend getting it fixed up in the draft forum. Also, make sure you look over some of the guides in the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/guide-hub" target="_blank">guide hub.</a></p>

							</div>

								
					
