			<div class="content" id="post-content-3839505">
									

<p>Upvoting, but I've got some big complaints. One I feel is just my personal opinions, and nothing to be done about that; but the other, I feel is without explanation or just out of foundation character.</p>
<p>The first bit: I feel like gamers against weed is going down the are we cool yet and wondertainment road of overuse as a goi. It's getting to the point where it just feels like its tacked on, like, why can't there be other online communities of individuals like this, why is it always them.</p>
<p>But that's just me, and I know plenty of people have no problem with it.</p>
<p>Now, the second problem: why is it just assumed that closing or destroying the school would cause it to move elsewhere? Why is the researcher just assuming this? Is there precedence? Did someone tell them this? Because as it stands there is no reason indicated that it would be like this. I can't imagine the foundation wouldn't have tried to close the school on some fabricated basis to see whether removing public access to see if it would contain it from the public. It would make sense to me if they tried to do this and found it starting to appear elsewhere, leading them to re-open the school and expand their janitorial activities to both places, or leaving the school shut down and moving the janitor operation there. I know the purpose of this is to justify why they are patrolling hallways for these, and that's fine, but as it is it doesn't make sense in universe.</p>
<p>Overall though, I liked it. At least enough to +1.</p>

